### Detailed Blueprint for Employee Role UI - Integrating into Current Layout

#### 1. Main Header (Untouched)

*   **Content:** "DOCUMENT SOLUTIONS" (or similar system name).
*   **Functionality:** Not explicitly detailed, but generally holds the system logo, name, and possibly global utility icons (e.g., help, feedback).

#### 2. Left Sidebar (For Left Sidebar Options)

This area will house the core navigation for the Employee, as previously defined. It should be collapsible/expandable to optimize screen real estate.

*   **Component:** A standard navigation menu component (e.g., `<ul>` with `<li>` items, or a specialized sidebar component from a UI library).
*   **Styling:** Should clearly indicate the currently active (selected) navigation item. Icons next to each item are highly recommended for visual clarity.
*   **Content (Employee Specific):**
    *   **Dashboard** (Icon: Home/Dashboard)
    *   **Documents** (Icon: Folder/Document stack)
    *   **Notifications** (Icon: Bell/Alert)
    *   **Shared With Me** (Icon: Share/Users)
    *   **My Workflows** (Icon: Workflow/Process)

#### 3. Top-Center Navigation Header (TOP BAR FUNCTIONALITY)

This area is ideal for context-sensitive actions, search, and user-specific controls that are not part of the main header.

*   **Component:** A horizontal navigation/action bar.
*   **Content:**
    *   **1. Global Search Bar:**
        *   **Placement:** Prominently on the left side of this header.
        *   **Functionality:** A text input field (`<input type="search">`).
            *   **Scope:** Defaults to "All accessible documents." Can have a small dropdown/toggle next to it to switch scope to "Current Folder" (if in Documents view).
            *   **Behavior:** As the user types, suggestions can appear (document names, tags, document types). Pressing Enter performs a full search, displaying results in the Main Content Area.
            *   **Data Source:** Searches `dms_document.name`, `dms_document.description`, `dms_document.extracted_text`, and associated `dms_tag.name` for documents the `current_user_id` has `view` permission for.
    *   **2. Contextual Actions/Breadcrumbs (Dynamic):**
        *   **Placement:** Central, to the right of the search bar.
        *   **Functionality:** This area dynamically updates based on the Left Sidebar selection and current navigation within a section.
            *   **"Home / Dashboard" selected:** Might display "Dashboard Overview."
            *   **"Documents" selected & folder navigated:** Displays breadcrumbs (e.g., `Home > Department X > Project Y`), each clickable to navigate back up the hierarchy.
            *   **"Documents" selected & document opened:** Displays `Documents > [Folder Name] > [Document Name]`.
            *   **"Notifications" selected:** Displays "Notifications."
            *   **"Shared With Me" selected:** Displays "Shared With Me."
            *   **"My Workflows" selected:** Displays "My Workflows."
    *   **3. User Controls (Right-aligned):**
        *   **Placement:** Far right of the header.
        *   **Content:**
            *   **User Avatar/Icon:** Clicking opens a dropdown menu.
            *   **Username Display:** (e.g., "John Doe").
            *   **Dropdown Menu Items:**
                *   "My Profile" (link to personal settings/profile view).
                *   "Change Password."
                *   "Logout."
            *   **Unread Notifications Badge:** A small numerical badge over a bell icon, showing the count of unread notifications for `current_user_id`. Clicking it can either navigate to the "Notifications" page or display a quick popover of recent notifications.

#### 4. Main Content Area

This area is where the dynamic content for each Left Sidebar selection will be rendered.

##### A. Main Content for "Home / Dashboard"

*   **Layout:** A flexible grid layout using cards or distinct sections for each widget.
*   **Content:**
    *   **Section 1: "Welcome, [Employee's First Name]!"**
        *   Large, friendly text.
        *   **Component:** `<h1>` or `<h2>` tag for the greeting.
    *   **Section 2: "My Pending Tasks" (Interactive List/Table)**
        *   **Component:** A data table with clear columns and interactive rows.
        *   **Header:** "My Pending Tasks" with an optional "View All" link to "My Workflows" (filtered for pending).
        *   **Columns:** `Document Name` (linked), `Task Name`, `Assigned By`, `Due Date`.
        *   **Row Interaction:** Clicking a row (or a dedicated "Action" button within the row) navigates to the associated document and immediately brings up the **"Complete Task" modal (described under My Workflows main content).**
        *   **Visuals:** `Due Date` styling (red for overdue, yellow for nearing due date).
        *   **Data Source:** Top 5-7 `dms_workflowtask` entries for `current_user_id` where `status = 'PENDING'`, ordered by `dms_workflowtask.due_date` ASC.
    *   **Section 3: "Recently Viewed Documents" (Card/List View)**
        *   **Component:** A list or small card component.
        *   **Header:** "Recently Viewed Documents."
        *   **Items:** Each item shows `document.name` (linked), `document.folder.name`, `document.updated_at`.
        *   **Data Source:** Top 5-7 `dms_user_activity` (derived from audit logs for `VIEW_DOCUMENT` or `EDIT_DOCUMENT` actions for the `current_user_id`).
    *   **Section 4: "My Recent Uploads" (List View)**
        *   **Component:** A simple list.
        *   **Header:** "My Recent Uploads."
        *   **Items:** Each item shows `document.name` (linked), `document.created_at`, `document.document_type.name`.
        *   **Data Source:** Top 3-5 `dms_document` entries where `uploader_id = current_user_id`, ordered by `created_at` DESC.
    *   **Section 5: "System Announcements" (Text Panel)**
        *   **Component:** A scrollable text or carousel panel.
        *   **Header:** "Important Announcements."
        *   **Content:** Latest active announcements with `title` and short excerpt.

##### B. Main Content for "Documents"

*   **Layout:** Three main columnar sections. The "Folder Tree View" will be part of this main content area, rather than a separate Left Sidebar item. The "Right Sidebar" will hold the document-specific details previously in the "Right Property Panel."
    *   **Left Column (Within Main Content): "Folder Tree View"**
        *   **Component:** An interactive tree view.
        *   **Functionality:**
            *   **Data Source:** Hierarchical display of `dms_folder`s where `current_user_id` has `view` permission.
            *   **Interaction:** Clicking a folder node loads its contents into the "Central Document List." Context menu (right-click or icon) for folder-specific actions (e.g., "Create Sub-folder", "Share Folder").
    *   **Central Column (Within Main Content): "Document List & Controls"**
        *   **Top Sub-bar:**
            *   **"Upload Document" Button:** Prominently placed. **Visibility:** Only if `add_document` permission exists for the current folder.
                *   **Action:** Opens a modal for document upload (file input, `document.name`, `description`, `document_type_id`, `correspondent_id`, `tags`, optional "Start Workflow").
            *   **Filters & Sorts:** Dropdowns for `document_type`, `correspondent`, `tag`, `uploader`, `date_range`. Sorting by `name`, `upload_date`, `updated_at`, `file_size`.
        *   **Main Display:** A data table or grid view.
            *   **Sub-folders List:** (If any) `folder.name` (linked), `owner`, `updated_at`.
            *   **Documents Table/Grid:**
                *   **Columns:** `Name` (linked), `Type`, `Uploader`, `Last Updated`, `Version`, `Locked By`, `Tags`.
                *   **Row Interaction:** Clicking `Name` or a "View" button will open the document in the embedded viewer (in the Right Sidebar) and update its tabs. Selecting a row will update the Right Sidebar.
                *   **Context Menu (on document row):** (Triggered by ellipsis icon or right-click).
                    *   **View, Edit, Download, Share, Lock/Unlock, Version History, Add Tag, Add Annotation/Comment, Start Workflow, Delete, Move/Copy.** (Visibility and enablement based on `guardian` permissions for `current_user_id` and specific `dms_document`).
    *   **No Right Property Panel here:** Its functionality is absorbed by the dedicated Right Sidebar.

##### C. Main Content for "Notifications"

*   **Layout:** A single, central data table or list component.
*   **Content:**
    *   **Top Bar (within Main Content):**
        *   **"Mark All as Read" Button.**
        *   **"Clear All Read Notifications" Button.**
        *   **Filter:** Dropdown for "All," "Unread," "Read."
    *   **Notifications Table:**
        *   **Columns:** `Status` (icon for read/unread), `Message`, `Timestamp`, `Actions`.
        *   **Action Column:** "View Item" button (navigates to `notification.link_to_item`), "Mark Read/Unread" toggle, "Delete" button.
        *   **Visuals:** Unread notifications styled distinctly.
        *   **Data Source:** All `dms_notification` for `current_user_id`, ordered by `created_at` DESC.

##### D. Main Content for "Shared With Me"

*   **Layout:** A single, central data table.
*   **Content:**
    *   **Top Bar (within Main Content):**
        *   **Filter Toggle:** Buttons for "Documents" / "Folders."
        *   **Search Input:** Search within shared items.
    *   **Shared Items Table:**
        *   **Columns:** `Item Name` (linked), `Item Type`, `Shared By`, `My Permission`, `Shared On`, `Expires On`, `Actions`.
        *   **Visuals:** Highlight expired/expiring items.
        *   **Action Column:** "View," "Edit," "Download" (visibility based on `permission_level`).
        *   **Data Source:** `dms_shareditem` entries where `shared_with_user_id = current_user_id` or `current_user_id` is in `shared_with_group_id`.

##### E. Main Content for "My Workflows"

*   **Layout:** A single, central data table.
*   **Content:**
    *   **Top Bar (within Main Content):**
        *   **Filter Options:** Dropdowns for `status` ("All", "Pending", "Completed", etc.), `due_date` range.
        *   **Search Input:** Search by `document.name` or `workflow_step.name`.
    *   **My Tasks Table:**
        *   **Columns:** `Document Name` (linked), `Workflow Name`, `Current Step`, `Status`, `Assigned On`, `Due Date`, `Completed On`, `Actions`.
        *   **Visuals:** `Due Date` highlighting for overdue/nearing due.
        *   **Action Column:**
            *   **"View Document" Button.**
            *   **"Complete Task" Button (for PENDING tasks):**
                *   **Action:** Opens a modal:
                    *   `Required Action` text display.
                    *   `Action Taken` (dropdown/radio: Approve, Reject, Complete, Edit & Complete).
                    *   `Comment` (textarea).
                    *   "Submit" button.
            *   **"Request Clarification" Button (for PENDING tasks):** Opens a modal to send a notification to the workflow initiator.
            *   **"View Details" Button (for completed/rejected tasks):** Shows `action_taken` and `comment`.
        *   **Data Source:** All `dms_workflowtask` for `assigned_to_id = current_user_id`.

#### 5. Right Sidebar (Fixed with Tabs: Properties, Action Buttons, Quick Links)

This fixed sidebar needs to dynamically update its content based on what is selected in the "Main Content Area," particularly when a document or folder is selected in the "Documents" view, or a task in "My Workflows."

*   **Component:** A tabbed interface component within a fixed sidebar.
*   **Tabs:**
    *   **1. Properties Tab**
        *   **Functionality:**
            *   **No item selected:** Display "Select a document or folder to view properties."
            *   **Folder selected (in Documents):**
                *   **Content:** `Folder Name`, `Parent Folder`, `Owner`, `Created At`, `Updated At`, `Is Active`.
                *   **Actions:** "Edit Folder Metadata" (if `edit_folder` permission).
            *   **Document selected (in Documents or other views):**
                *   **Content:** All document metadata: `document.name`, `document.description`, `document_type.name`, `correspondent.name`, `uploader.username`, `created_at`, `updated_at`, `tags` (clickable), `document.rating` (average).
                *   **Annotations/Comments:** A sub-section listing `dms_annotation`s for the `current_version`, with `user`, `content`, `page_number`, `created_at`. An "Add Annotation/Comment" input field (if `add_annotation` permission).
                *   **Workflow Status:** (If document is in a workflow) `dms_workflowinstance.status`, `current_step.name`, `initiated_by.username`, timeline of `dms_workflowtask`s.
                *   **Actions:** "Edit Metadata" button (if `edit_document` permission).
            *   **Workflow Task selected (in My Workflows):**
                *   **Content:** `Document Name`, `Workflow Template Name`, `Current Step Name`, `Assigned To`, `Status`, `Assigned At`, `Due Date`, `Completed At`, `Action Taken`, `Comment`.
    *   **2. Action Buttons Tab**
        *   **Functionality:** Provides context-sensitive actions for the currently selected item. This consolidates many actions previously in document/folder context menus or embedded within view modals.
            *   **No item selected:** Display "Select an item to see available actions."
            *   **Folder selected (in Documents):**
                *   **Buttons:** "Create Sub-folder" (if `add_folder` permission), "Upload Document" (if `add_document`), "Share Folder" (if `share_folder`), "Delete Folder" (if `delete_folder`). (Each only visible/enabled if permissions allow).
            *   **Document selected (in Documents or other views):**
                *   **Buttons:** "View Document," "Edit Document," "Download," "Share," "Lock/Unlock," "Version History," "Add Tag," "Add Annotation," "Start Workflow," "Delete Document," "Move/Copy." (Each only visible/enabled if permissions and document status allow, e.g., "Edit" disabled if locked by another user).
            *   **Workflow Task selected (in My Workflows):**
                *   **Buttons:** "View Document," "Complete Task" (if pending), "Request Clarification" (if pending).
    *   **3. Quick Links Tab**
        *   **Functionality:** Provides quick access to common system areas or user-specific frequently used links. These are mostly static or semi-static.
            *   **Content (Employee Specific):**
                *   "My Profile" (link)
                *   "Settings" (link to personal preferences)
                *   "Help Documentation" (external link)
                *   "Report an Issue" (link to a feedback/support form)
                *   "Recently Deleted Documents" (link to a recycle bin-like view, if implemented for soft-deleted items by the user).
                *   Dynamic links, e.g., "Link to Department Wiki" (if configured by admin).

